From 24787006862c80fd8046e1ee3b32999fa46d2f56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:25:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] x11: speak XDND version 3, and send what each version
 needs

Drags announced XDND version 2.  The specification's change log
(1998-09-07) says compliance requires version 3 and up, and GTK ignores an
XdndEnter that says less ("Ignored old XdndEnter message" with
GDK_DEBUG=dnd), so nothing dragged out of a GNUstep application could be
dropped on a GTK application.  Version 3 only changed where XdndAware is
placed (on the top-level window, not subwindows), which is where this
backend already puts it.

Raising the version showed that dnd_version_at_least() compared the wrong
way round: ((a) <= (b)), called as (dragging_version, 1) for the time
stamps and (dragging_version, 2) for the action.  At version 2 a drag sent
the action but never a time stamp; at version 3 it would send neither, and
GTK sees no action and refuses the drop.  It now compares (a) >= (b), so
XdndPosition and XdndDrop carry the time stamp from version 1 and
XdndPosition the action from version 2, as the specification says.

XdndStatus is sent when a GNUstep window is the drop target, and the
target side never records the source's version (dragging_version is
whatever the application's last drag left, 0 at first).  With the corrected
comparison it would stop sending the accepted action to every source.  It
now sends the action whenever it accepts, as it did before for every
version up to 2; versions before 2 treat that field as reserved.

Testing: Tests/x11/xdndversion.m includes xdnd.c, as the other x11 tests
include the sources they test, and sends the messages with its functions
to a window the test created, then reads the ClientMessage back from its
own connection.  It checks that the version is 3 or more; that at
version 3 XdndPosition has the time and the action and XdndDrop the time;
that at version 1 XdndPosition has the time and no action, and at
version 0 neither; and that XdndStatus has the action when it accepts
(with dragging_version 0) and none when it refuses.  That covers the new
version, each version-dependent field on both sides of the comparison,
and guards the target side against the change.  Without this change 5 of
the 7 checks fail (the two XdndStatus checks pass); with it all 7 pass.
The whole suite, each backend loaded alone from a private GNUstep.conf on
Xvfb: 300 passed, none failed, against 295 passed and these 5 failed
before it; pdfps.m aborts the same way on both, in the installed libs-gui
snapshot's font roles.

Under GNOME Shell (X11, Xvfb) with Nautilus as the drop target, a file
dragged out of a GNUstep application with this change and the previous
one is copied into the folder, byte for byte.  GTK's log shows version 3
in XdndEnter, the drag's types (text/uri-list), XdndPosition with the
copy action and a time, two refused portal types, then text/uri-list read.
Without this change GTK ignores the drag; with it but without the
previous change GTK asks for TARGETS and gets no answer.

Not covered: a GNUstep window as the drop target of a GTK drag; the
editable text view tried in the run above takes no file drops with or
without these changes, so it showed nothing either way.  XdndEnter still
announces the backend's version rather than min(source, target); every
compliant target supports version 3, so the two agree.  The time stamps
in XdndPosition come from the drag loop's NSEvents; XdndDrop's is the
release event's.

AI assistance: this change, its test and this description were written
with Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Headers/x11/xdnd.h |  6 +++++-
 Source/x11/xdnd.c  | 10 ++++++----
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Headers/x11/xdnd.h b/Headers/x11/xdnd.h
index 20d94e4..0a8c508 100644
--- a/Headers/x11/xdnd.h
+++ b/Headers/x11/xdnd.h
@@ -24,7 +24,11 @@
 #ifndef _X_DND_H
 #define _X_DND_H
 
-#define XDND_VERSION 2
+/* XDND compliance starts at version 3; GTK ignores a drag that says
+ * less.  Version 3 only moved XdndAware to the top-level window, where
+ * this backend already puts it.
+ */
+#define XDND_VERSION 3
 
 /* XdndEnter */
 #define XDND_THREE 3
diff --git a/Source/x11/xdnd.c b/Source/x11/xdnd.c
index 94abd51..fa6bd6b 100644
--- a/Source/x11/xdnd.c
+++ b/Source/x11/xdnd.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 
 
 // #define DND_DEBUG 
-#define dnd_version_at_least(a,b) ((a) <= (b))
+#define dnd_version_at_least(a,b) ((a) >= (b))
 
 #ifdef DND_DEBUG
 #define dnd_debug(a,b...) printf("%s: %d: " a "\n", __FILE__, __LINE__ , ## b)
@@ -240,9 +240,11 @@ xdnd_send_status(DndClass *dnd, Window window, Window from, int will_accept,
     XDND_STATUS_WANT_POSITION_SET (&xevent, want_position);
   if (want_position)
     XDND_STATUS_RECT_SET (&xevent, x, y, w, h);
-  if (dnd_version_at_least (dnd->dragging_version, 2))
-    if (will_accept)
-      XDND_STATUS_ACTION (&xevent) = action;
+  /* Sent as a drop target, which doesn't know the source's version;
+   * versions before 2 treat this field as reserved.
+   */
+  if (will_accept)
+    XDND_STATUS_ACTION (&xevent) = action;
 
   XSendEvent (dnd->display, window, 0, 0, &xevent);
 }
